      "text": "To solve the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\), we first need to take the square root of both sides. This step reveals the two potential solutions to the equation: \\(x - 5 = 3\\) and \\(x - 5 = -3\\). Solving these two equations for \\(x\\) will give us the roots of the equation.\n\nThe equation \\(x - 5 = 3\\) yields \\(x = 8\\), and the equation \\(x - 5 = -3\\) yields \\(x = 2\\). So, the roots of the original equation are \\(8\\) and \\(2\\).\n\nTo find the sum of these roots, we simply add \\(8\\) and \\(2\\):\n\n\\[ 8 + 2 = 10 \\]\n\nThus, the sum of the roots of the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).\n\nHere is the Python code to verify this:\n\n```python\n# Define the equation\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\nx = sp.symbols('x')\n\n# Define the equation (x - 5)^2 = 9\nequation = (x - 5)**2 - 9\n\n# Solve the equation for x\nroots = sp.solve(equation, x)\n\n# Calculate the sum of the roots\nsum_of_roots = sum(roots)\n\nprint(sum_of_roots)\n```",
